## Preflight rulings

1. Schema v3 stays readable for audit only. All new resumable/runtime behavior is schema v4; old scores and identities are never reinterpreted.
2. `PIT_NON_TRADABLE_REFERENCE_SYMBOLS` uses canonical provenance order `(IWM, QQQ, SPY)`, while `MarketContextV1.benchmarks` deliberately uses policy presentation order `(SPY, QQQ, IWM)`. Conversion is explicit; neither order is inferred from the other.
3. “Three calls per complete iteration” means three declared plan slots. A recoverable invalid investigator may settle author/critic slots as authenticated skips; skips consume zero calls and no usage.
4. The only rank/return gate is quantized absolute portfolio CAGR. Drawdown, trades, Sharpe, turnover, baseline delta, and other values remain diagnostics and integrity evidence only.
5. Task 4 owns qualification-ledger initialization, authentication, immutable snapshot, and retired-lineage exclusion. Task 9 extends the same contract with reservation/outcome mutation; it must not fork a second ledger model.
6. Qualification-plan contents remain separate and unavailable to search roles/controller. Search sees only its commitment.
7. Task 8 may import candidate source/checkpoint state but must remint identity and reevaluate under a changed plan; old evaluation scores never seed a new champion directly.
8. Task 10 may use the plan's data-only Alpaca SIP reference backfill, but makes no OpenRouter calls. Task 11 is the only live role-call task.
9. S&P-only qualification/canary results are architecture evidence. `full_replay_ready` remains false until a separate authenticated S&P/Nasdaq/Russell constituent bundle exists.
10. No tracked candidate policy source is applied, no full replay starts, and no Git push/upload occurs in this execution plan.
11. User speed override (2026-09-01): production-first implementation; no test-first design, no broad per-task suites, and no prolonged review cycles absent a concrete blocker. Use focused smoke checks and short scoped reviews. Provider accounting, credential/data secrecy, causal evaluation integrity, disposable execution, `apply=false`, and zero retries remain non-negotiable correctness boundaries.

